# Evaluation output. The timestamped history is regenerated on every run and
# does not belong in version control, but `latest.*` IS committed: the README
# and docs link to it, and a reviewer should be able to read the measured
# results without installing anything first.
# Timestamped runs are local noise; the "latest" of each configuration is
# tracked, because docs/evaluation.md quotes numbers from them and a reader
# has to be able to check them.
evaluation/reports/*
!evaluation/reports/.gitkeep
!evaluation/reports/latest.md
!evaluation/reports/latest.json
!evaluation/reports/nli/
!evaluation/reports/ollama/
!evaluation/reports/ollama-nli/
evaluation/reports/*/evaluation-*


